# __PACKAGE_NAME__

GENERATED npm package candidate — do not hand-edit. Regenerate via `python3 compiler/tools/regen_all.py` in the DeliberateCode/System2 repo.

System2 is a deliberate-reasoning workflow for the [Pi coding agent](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-coding-agent). This candidate contains the compiler-generated base workflow, prompts, and safety extension. It has no install scripts or dependencies.

## Availability

This package is **pending publication**. There is no supported npm installation command, and the package name must not be treated as currently installable.

## Materialize project files

After publication, the package's `/system2-init` command will materialize `AGENTS.md`, `.pi/SYSTEM.md`, and `system2.pi.lock.json` into the current project. Re-running is idempotent: byte-identical files are skipped, locally modified files are left untouched unless `--force` is supplied, paths outside the project root are refused, and unmanaged files are never touched.

## Scope

The candidate contains the **base 13-role workflow** composed with an empty overlay set. `/delegate` switches roles in-session; it is not native isolated subagent execution.

Overlays and profiles are not end-user package UX. Applying them requires the source compiler; the published package will contain no compiler and will read no overlay input at install time or runtime.

## Enforcement fidelity

The Pi extension registers a `tool_call` handler that blocks declared shell, write-lease, and sensitive-path cases before execution. Budget reporting is adapted, while formatting and type-checking remain advisory. See `system2.pi.lock.json` for the per-capability report.

**Known limitation:** sensitive-path protection scans the entire shell command without an override, so sensitive tokens in otherwise benign command text can trigger a block.

